<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mound Key</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Calos</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mound Key is an island in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estero-bay">Estero Bay</a> on the south-west coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a>, built up largely of shell mounds by the Calusa. It is identified with Calos, the capital of the Calusa paramount chief, where the Spanish governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-menendez-de-aviles">Pedro Menéndez de Avilés</a> met the chief Carlos in 1566 and founded a short-lived <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuit</a> mission. It is now a state archaeological park.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mound-key.jpg" alt="Mound Key" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: State of Florida · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MoundKeyShellMound.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
